      "role": "user",
      "content": "i already tried telling my supervisor but they just thought i was burnt out from the long hours and told me to go home and sleep it off. but it's not just \"seeing things\"... it's too consistent. like yesterday i saw these heavy red clouds around a cyclist in the street and five minutes later a car clipped them. it wasn't a hallucination, it was like i was seeing the probability of it happening before it did. please dont just tell me to go to a doctor, i need to know if there's a scientific basis for how particles could actually alter how the brain processes temporal probability.",
